==============================================================================
[2] FREE FIELD chi_L  (shell counting, max-norm, must saturate ~ C L^2)
==============================================================================
chi_L = sum_{x in T^4_L, x != 0} 1/(4 pi^2 |x|^2), |x| = max-norm on Z^4
  L=  8  chi_L=     17.0557   chi_L/L^2=  0.2665
  L= 16  chi_L=     59.4625   chi_L/L^2=  0.2323
  L= 32  chi_L=    221.8451   chi_L/L^2=  0.2166
  L= 64  chi_L=    857.6062   chi_L/L^2=  0.2094
  L=128  chi_L=   3373.8916   chi_L/L^2=  0.2059
=> chi_L/L^2 decays only logarithmically (0.267 -> 0.206, drifts like 1/log L)
   => chi_L = Theta(L^2) (bounded away from 0 and from infinity when divided by L^2)
   so H1 FAILS on the free field (Q6:183), while P HOLDS. => H1 is strictly stronger than P.
   Check: H1 => P is exact: plateau mass r0 at m<=sqrt(c)/L gives chi >= r0 L^2/c -> infinity.

