==============================================================================
[8] H1 => P (exact algebra) and (P + atom) => no light mode
==============================================================================
plateau with mass r0 in {m <= sqrt(c)/L}:  chi = int s^{-1} dnu >= r0 / (c/L^2) = r0 L^2 / c
   r0=0.50 c=1.0 L=   8 :  r0 L^2/c =    32.0000   (grows like L^2)
   r0=0.50 c=1.0 L=  64 :  r0 L^2/c =  2048.0000   (grows like L^2)
   r0=0.50 c=1.0 L=1024 :  r0 L^2/c = 524288.0000   (grows like L^2)
   r0=0.10 c=4.0 L= 256 :  r0 L^2/c =  1638.4000   (grows like L^2)
=> any plateau forces chi_L >= r0 L^2/c -> infinity, i.e. contradicts H1 (chi <= 1/lambda).
   Hence  H1 => P  [T],  and P does NOT imply H1 (free field: P true, H1 false).
   (P + f1^2 >= r0) => no light mode: a light atom of weight >= r0 IS cumulative mass >= r0
   inside {m <= sqrt(c)/L} for every fixed c -> plateau -> violates P.  [T]

